<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Bancomext to lend $10 bln in 1997.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Bancomext to lend $10 bln in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>GUADALAJARA, Mexico 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's state National Export Bank (Bancomext) said on Monday it plans to lend some $10 billion to export-oriented companies this year compared to about $6.3 billion last year.</p>
<p>Bancomext director general Enrique Vilatela Riba said the state bank will focus on lending to companies that have never exported but want to take part in the country's growing exports.</p>
<p>-- Monica Ballesca, Guadalajara bureau +523 817-0397</p>
